---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="REPL Works"
  description="REPL Works is an AI-Native Product Development Framework for building projects with durable memory, model independence, and Git-native continuity."
>
  <section class="space-y-10">
    <div
      class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm sm:p-12"
    >
      <p
        class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-500"
      >
        AI-Native Product Development Framework
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-6xl"
      >
        Build projects that remember.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">
        REPL Works keeps product work durable with project memory, model
        independence, Git-native development, context compression, and long-term
        project continuity.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
        <a
          href="/workflow"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-900 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-slate-800"
        >
          Learn the Workflow
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/replworks/replworks.github.io"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-slate-300 bg-white px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 transition hover:border-slate-400 hover:bg-slate-50"
        >
          View GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm"
      >
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Project Memory</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-7">
          Capture decisions, constraints, and intent in durable documents
          instead of leaving them in chat history.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm"
      >
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
          Model Independence
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-7">
          Switch models without losing the project structure that keeps work
          understandable and reviewable.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm"
      >
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
          Git-Native Development
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-7">
          Keep product memory in versioned Markdown so every change can be
          reviewed, committed, and traced.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm"
      >
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
          Context Compression
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-7">
          Compress project history into the smallest set of documents needed for
          the next decision or task.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm md:col-span-2 xl:col-span-1"
      >
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
          Long-Term Continuity
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-7">
          Preserve momentum across sessions, contributors, and release cycles
          without rebuilding context from scratch.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
        Start with the workflow
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-slate-600 leading-7">
        The best entry point is the workflow, because it shows how REPL Works
        moves from idea refinement to operation through documents, discussion
        AI, execution AI, and human review.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="/workflow"
          class="rounded-full bg-slate-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 transition hover:bg-slate-200"
        >
          Workflow
        </a>
        <a
          href="/documents"
          class="rounded-full bg-slate-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 transition hover:bg-slate-200"
        >
          Documents
        </a>
        <a
          href="/prompts"
          class="rounded-full bg-slate-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 transition hover:bg-slate-200"
        >
          Prompts
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
